            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Malayalam for an itinerary, then the Malayalam for to roam around."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: അലയുക",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "അലയുക — alayuka — \"to wander; to roam\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "വഴി അറിയാതെ ഞങ്ങൾ ഒരു മണിക്കൂർ അലഞ്ഞു. vaḻi aṟiyāte ñaṅṅaḷ oru maṇikkūr alaññu. Not knowing the way, we wandered for an hour."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past: അലഞ്ഞു, alaññu."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It means wandering without a plan, often tired or lost."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "അലയുക (alayuka) is native Dravidian; DEDR gives the Malayalam verb as to be tossed about and to roam (DEDR 240)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
        },
