          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "സഹയാത്രികൻ — sahayātrikan — \"a fellow traveller\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "തീവണ്ടിയിലെ സഹയാത്രികൻ എനിക്ക് ഒരു പഴം തന്നു. tīvaṇṭiyile sahayātrikan enikkŭ oru paḻaṁ tannu. My fellow traveller on the train gave me a banana."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: സഹയാത്രികർ, sahayātrikar."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "സഹ- means with, as in സഹപാഠി, a classmate."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "സഹയാത്രികൻ (sahayātrikan) is built from Sanskrit saha, \"with\", and yātrika, \"relating to a journey\" (Monier-Williams), with the masculine ending -ൻ."
            }
