          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ഇടത്താവളം — iṭattāvaḷaṁ — \"a stopover; a halting place\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ആ ചെറിയ ഗ്രാമം ഞങ്ങളുടെ യാത്രയിലെ ഇടത്താവളമായിരുന്നു. ā ceṟiya grāmaṁ ñaṅṅaḷuṭe yātrayile iṭattāvaḷamāyirunnu. That small village was the stopover on our journey."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ഇട means the middle, as in ഇടയിൽ, between; താവളം is a camp or a place to stay."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ഇടത്താവളം (iṭattāvaḷaṁ) is a Malayalam compound built from the native ഇട, the middle or interval (DEDR 448), and താവളം, a camp or lodging; the origin of താവളം is not settled."
            }
          ]
        },
